 "exercise": {
  "id": "pqp03-ex07",
  "chapter": 3,
  "number": "3.7",
  "title": "Diagram substitution",
  "level": 2,
  "statement": "Two H boxes in a row are a plain wire: $H H = 1$ (you will see why in Chapter 5). Use this equation to get from the proof's given first step to its given last step.\n\n- Select D₁ and press **＋ Step**: a copy appears as the next step.\n- In the diagram **H H = 1** (right), select the plain wire and copy it (Cmd/Ctrl+C).\n- In your new step, select both H boxes (Shift-click) and paste (Cmd/Ctrl+V): the pair is replaced by the wire, reconnected in order — the \"same place\" rule of PQP Remark 3.16.\n- Write the rule you used in the step's **rule…** box.\n\nAfterwards, try the one-click way: select the two H boxes and look in the inspector for *Cancel H·H*.",
  "done": "The Exercise panel shows ✓ Solved.",
  "book": "textbook/ch03.html#ex-3-7"
 }
